# APNs Registration Fix Required

## Problem:
iOS/macOS apps are not registering for push notifications, so no APNs tokens are obtained or sent to backend.

## Required Steps:

### 1. Check Xcode Configuration
- Verify APNs certificates are added to Xcode project
- Check bundle IDs match Apple Developer certificates
- Ensure push notifications capability is enabled

### 2. Check App Permissions
- Launch iOS/macOS apps
- Grant notification permissions when prompted
- Check Settings → Notifications → TimeBeam → Allow

### 3. Monitor Registration Process
- Check Xcode console for permission request logs
- Look for "Requesting notification permissions" messages
- Verify "Successfully registered for remote notifications" logs
- Check for APNs token logs

### 4. Verify Backend Communication
- Check backend logs for APNs token update API calls
- Verify tokens are stored in user_devices table
- Confirm has_token = true for devices

### 5. Test Notification Delivery
- Start timer on one device
- Check backend sends APNs to other devices
- Verify receiving device processes notification
- Confirm timer starts automatically

## Code is Ready:
- Apps have proper notification registration code ✅
- Backend can send APNs notifications ✅
- Timer sync APIs work ✅

## Issue is Configuration/Runtime:
- APNs certificates may not be properly configured
- User permissions may be denied
- Apps may not be running to register tokens